// Warm start ACROSS a changed species list, and a kal column added in a
// later start (review findings 42 + 44, 7 Oct 2026).
// Start 1: a restricted (A)20 slab in a mirror box (chi 1.2, membrane seed;
// phi max 0.75). Start 2 adds ONLY a trace free monomer B at phibulk 1e-4.
// Before the fix a changed iteration-species list cold-started the solve:
// u = 0 is an exact fixed point of a restricted molecule in a mirror box,
// so start 2 "converged in 0 iterations" on the UNIFORM state (phi 0.2
// everywhere, F -0.145) although that state lies inside the spinodal. Now
// the potentials are copied by species NAME and B starts at u = 0 (what
// Namics' Guess does): start 2 stays on the slab, F -1.330 vs start 1's
// -1.293 (the additive's small perturbation). Namics also keeps start 2
// structured (oracle phi max 0.78; its own start 1 lands elsewhere from
// its membrane guess, so the F values are not an oracle pair).
// The kal line added in start 2 (pol phibulk) is a column of the WHOLE
// file, filled in start 1's row too -- the Namics behaviour (oracle-checked
// on the same layout: one header, rectangular rows). Before the fix the
// header kept start 1's two columns while row 2 had three fields.
lat : flat : geometry : flat
lat : flat : n_layers : 40
lat : flat : lowerbound : mirror
lat : flat : upperbound : mirror
lat : flat : lattice_type : simple_cubic
mon : A : freedom : free
mon : W : freedom : free
mon : A : chi_W : 1.2
mol : W : composition : (W)1
mol : W : freedom : solvent
mol : pol : composition : (A)20
mol : pol : freedom : restricted
mol : pol : theta : 8
sys : NN : initial_guess : membrane
output : kal : append : false
kal : mol : pol : theta
kal : sys : NN : free_energy
output : pro : append : false
pro : mol : pol : phi
start
mon : B : freedom : free
mol : add : composition : (B)1
mol : add : freedom : free
mol : add : phibulk : 1e-4
kal : mol : pol : phibulk
start
